# Bazel uses a Python-ish syntax. The load statement is somewhat equivalent
# to a Python module import.
# I.e. the next line makes the `ddk_module` function available for this file.
# We reference the file `build/kernel/kleaf/kernel.bzl` from the kernel source
# tree here.
# Check out the documentation [1] for more information.
#
# [1] https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/build/+/refs/heads/main/kleaf/docs/ddk/rules.md#ddk_module
load("//build/kernel/kleaf:kernel.bzl", "ddk_module")


# Module: aosp_training_random
#
# This is a "library" module.
# I.e. it does not provide any driver functionality and is not started by some
# `*init()` function but is invoked by other kernel code.
# It provides a single function to "generate" random numbers.
#
# You will have to enable (comment in) this module and add the missing line
# making the headers available to other modules.
